    "created_at": "2016-11-22T11:30:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-22T14:07:46Z",
    "body": "https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen/pull/64 keeps track of the original *topLevelDoc*, which isn't quite the same as keeping track of the node document. @upsuper, are pending Fullscreen requests in Gecko tied to each individual document, or a tab-wide manager of sorts?\r\n\r\nBlink has some state attached to the documents, but I'm trying to change things so that pending requests go into a single queue, although still in the same process as the documents. With per-document book keeping, I can't see how to get the order of requests right, if the same script requests fullscreen in two iframes for example.",
